From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:57:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/34] flashnext: --tp 2 prompt passes, mixed rounds and
 prompt tiles, each behind its own flag

Prompt-side work at --tp 2: a shared-prefix keep threshold for the prompt cache, batched keep frames, prompt chunks
queued without a drain, mixed rounds (a prompt piece inside a decode round's forward), split rank sums, sequence-
parallel rank sums and a row-split indexer for prompt passes, the MTP head's prompt rows on a side stream, wide HC
read-out tiles, an EXL3 fused rotation, bf16-once MXFP8 and FP8 mma prompt tiles, an mma indexer with fused top-k,
and a chunked DeltaNet prompt chain.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- feat(prompt-cache): TF_PCACHE_SHARED_MIN keeps a state where a new conversation parts from a kept one
- fix(prompt-cache): name the shared-prefix knob TENSORFOLD_PCACHE_SHARED_MIN
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_KEEP_BATCH=1 sends a round's --tp 2 keeps in one keep_many frame
- perf(flashnext): queue TP=2 prompt chunks without a per-chunk drain
- test(flashnext): wait for the async-coll guard's exit code, not only its flag
- perf(flashnext): mixed TP=2 rounds, a prompt piece in the decode round's forward
- test(flashnext): the async and mixed rank tests open RoCE as a served engine does
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_MS sizes a mixed round's prompt piece from its rounds' times
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SPLIT_SUM and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_OUT_PROMPT
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_LOOKUP=1 widens, weighs and chains context copies beside MTP
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR row-exchange rank sums for prompt passes
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_INDEX_ROWS row-split indexer for prompt passes
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_INDEX_MMA prompt indexer on mma tiles with fused top-k
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MTP_SIDE head rows of a prompt chunk on a side stream
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_WIDE read-out tiles: cluster split-K down, weight-stationary persistent up+mix
- flashnext exl3 prompt: TF_EXL3_FUSED_ROT, gate/up rotating its own input
- flashnext: bf16-once MXFP8 prompt tile, fused shared gate+up and FP8 mma prompt path, each default off
- flashnext: chunked DeltaNet prompt chain behind TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_CHUNKED

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TENSORFOLD_PCACHE_SHARED_MIN=<tokens> (native CUDA families; unset or 0: off) keeps one more state when a prompt
  shares at least that many tokens with a kept prompt: the state one token before they part, flagged shared, so a new
  conversation that shares an...
- TF_EXL3_FUSED_ROT=1 (TF_FLASHNEXT_EXPERTS_EXL3, passes on TF_EXL3_PROMPT_ROWS's kernels): the gate/up kernel rotates
  its input itself (exl3_fnx_prompt.cuh tf_exl3_fnx_gur), each block reading its members' bf16 rows and rotating one
  Hadamard block at a time...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_CHUNKED: added by the change "chunked DeltaNet prompt chain behind TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_CHUNKED".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HCW_DN / TF_FLASHNEXT_HCW_UP (with TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_WIDE): the row tile of the wide read-out's down and
  up+mix kernels; unset or 0: chosen by the pass's rows.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_WIDE: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_HC_WIDE read-out tiles: cluster split-K down,
  weight-stationary persistent up+mix".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_INDEX_MMA: this prompt pass selects from scores on mma tiles (flashnext_qsa_mma.cuh).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_MS=X (rank 0, 1 to 10000; unset or 0: off) sizes each piece from the last mixed rounds' times so
  a round's forward stays under X ms: it learns the time a piece row adds from two rounds of different rows, drops the
  rows a round overran by,...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_ROUNDS=1 (both ranks, drafting, TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_PARTIAL=1) lets a long prompt's middle piece
  of TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_ROWS rows (multiples of 64, default 256) wait for the next decode round and run in its
  forward.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_ROWS: a mixed round's prompt rows at most (multiples of 64 from 64 to 8192; unset 256).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_FP8MMA=1: the prompt tile's rows quantised to MXFP8 and multiplied on the block-scaled FP8 mma
  (qmmf8.zig).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_LOOKUP=1: the copies drafted from a stream's own context (lanes.SuffixLookup; on today at 15
  rows a shared round) widen in shared rounds as a lone stream's do, up to the 31 a window holds.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_LOOKUP_MIN=<n> (with TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_LOOKUP; 4 to 64, default 8): the matched context a
  context copy needs.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_SHARED_FUSED=1: a prompt pass's shared expert computes gate, up and SwiGLU in one launch
  (qmmf.cu shared_gu_body): each product summed in the lane kernel's K slices in its order and rounded to bf16, then
  fn_shared_swiglu's arithmetic, so...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_TILE2=1: the prompt tile's weights made bf16 once a block (prompt_t2_body; same sums, same
  bits).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_INDEX_ROWS: this pass's fused attention groups select a row half on each rank (cuda_index_rows.zig).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_KEEP_BATCH=1 (--tp 2): rank 0 rolls a window back on its own GPU at once and sends rank 1 a round's
  rollbacks in one keep_many frame ahead of its next command, whose ack it reads with that command's.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MTP_SIDE: added by the change "TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MTP_SIDE head rows of a prompt chunk on a side
  stream".
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_OUT_PROMPT=1 (--tp 2, TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE=2 and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_RELAXED=1): a prompt
  pass's out projection (DeltaNet out_proj, attention o_proj) takes the MXFP8 prompt tile one rank's takes (one fp32
  chain over K) for its part...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_ASYNC=1 (rank-local) queues a non-final prompt chunk at --tp 2 without draining it on either
  rank or waiting for rank 1's ack after it.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR: this pass's layers past the PLE layer exchange rows (cuda_seq_par.zig).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SPLIT_SUM: this pass's rank sums go in two row halves on s.sums' stream (cuda_split_sum.zig).
