+/// TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SPLIT_SUM=1 (--tp 2 with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_RELAXED=1; TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE=2 and
+/// TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_PARTIAL=1 for the sums it halves): a prompt pass of split_sum_min_rows rows or more adds the ranks'
+/// fp32 partials of the out projection and of the experts in two row halves on a stream of their own
+/// (cuda_split_sum.zig): the first half crosses the link while the second is computed, the second while the first
+/// half's write-back and read-out run. A two-rank sum is one add an element whatever rows a call holds, and every kernel
+/// around it computes a row alone, so the bits do not change; the ranks' collectives double in number, so both ranks
+/// must agree (bit 11 of tp_flags). A TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_ROUNDS piece keeps its sums whole on the pass's stream, whatever
+/// its rows: the round's windows issue collectives between its layers' sums. Unset or 0: one sum a site a layer on the
+/// pass's stream. Other values refuse to start (BadSplitSum).
+pub fn tpSplitSum() error{BadSplitSum}!bool {
+    return onOff(if (std.c.getenv("TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SPLIT_SUM")) |v| std.mem.span(v) else null) orelse error.BadSplitSum;
+}
