+/// TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR=1 (--tp 2 with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_RELAXED=1, TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE=2 and
+/// TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_PARTIAL=1): a prompt pass of split_sum_min_rows rows or more adds the ranks' fp32 partials past
+/// the PLE layer by row exchange (cuda_seq_par.zig). Each rank owns one row half: it sends the peer its partials of the
+/// peer's half and receives the peer's of its own, then writes back, reads out and routes its own half alone, and the
+/// ranks swap the read-out rows (and picks) the next split op reads over every row; the pass ends by swapping the
+/// streams and sums the head reads. A two-rank sum is one add an element in either order and every kernel around it
+/// computes a row alone, so the bits do not change. It changes what crosses the ranks, so both ranks must agree (bit 13
+/// of tp_flags). With TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SPLIT_SUM the peer's half is computed first and crosses the link on the sums'
+/// stream while this rank's own half is computed. A TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_ROUNDS piece keeps its sums whole (one all-reduce a
+/// site on the pass's stream), whatever its rows. Unset or 0: one all-reduce a site a layer. Other values refuse to
+/// start (BadSeqPar).
